# Scratch: one-off job scripts, SLURM logs and analysis helpers from cluster
# runs. Kept in-repo so they sit beside the work they describe, never
# committed -- they are noisy, machine-specific, and reference human-subjects
# audio paths. The README documents the convention so it survives a fresh
# clone; logs/.gitkeep makes scratch/logs/ exist in every clone, because SLURM
# will not create a job's log directory and a job whose log cannot be opened
# dies with no trace. hpc/ holds the tracked SLURM entry points.
/scratch/*
!/scratch/README.md
!/scratch/logs/
/scratch/logs/*
!/scratch/logs/.gitkeep

# Environment build recipes are source, not scratch. A global exclude on this
# machine ignores envs/ (the conda convention); the repo rule wins.
!/envs/
